## Getting Help

### Before Asking for Help

1. **Check the documentation**
    - [Getting Started](/getting-started/)
    - [How-To Guides](/guides/)
    - [Troubleshooting](/platform/troubleshooting/)
    - [Reference](/reference/)

2. **Search existing issues**
    - [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/rithum/pika/issues)
    - Someone may have already solved your problem

3. **Review common issues**
    - Check [Troubleshooting guide](/platform/troubleshooting/)
    - Look for similar error messages

---

## GitHub

### Issues

**[GitHub Issues](https://github.com/rithum/pika/issues)** - For bug reports and feature requests

#### Creating an Issue

When creating an issue, please include:

**For Bug Reports:**
- Clear description of the issue
- Steps to reproduce
- Expected vs actual behavior
- Environment details (OS, Node.js version, Pika version)
- Error messages and logs
- Screenshots if applicable

**For Feature Requests:**
- Clear description of the feature
- Use cases and benefits
- Proposed implementation (if you have ideas)
- Alternatives considered

### Discussions

**[GitHub Discussions](https://github.com/rithum/pika/discussions)** - For questions, ideas, and community chat

Use discussions for:
- General questions
- Sharing ideas
- Showing off projects
- Getting feedback
- Community discussions
- Best practices

### Pull Requests

Want to contribute code? See our [Contributing Guide](/platform/contributing/).

---

## Communication Channels

### GitHub (Primary)

- **Issues**: Bug reports and feature requests
- **Discussions**: Questions and community interaction
- **Pull Requests**: Code contributions

### Documentation Site

- **Guides**: Comprehensive how-to documentation
- **Reference**: API and configuration reference
- **Troubleshooting**: Common issues and solutions

